1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:24,219
For the first minute after Blue Thunder, my greatest achievement was
keeping breakfast inside my body. Nigga, nobody had put that part on
the poster. Shawna held a bottle of water to my mouth. My hands were
still shaking too hard to trust with it. Through the windshield I
could see students crossing the restored stadium road, helping one
another toward the helicopters.

2
00:00:24,469 --> 00:00:47,533
Every few steps somebody looked at my car and raised a hand. I raised
mine back. The fingers trembled. That did not make the wave less
important. Tank reached us first. He leaned through the window, saw my
face, and lost the joke he had brought with him. How bad? Nigga,
electricity got a terrible cancellation policy. He looked at Shawna.

3
00:00:47,783 --> 00:01:05,388
She shook her head once: tired, hurt, awake. He understood. Victor
landed beside the car and sat on the curb without pretending he had
meant to sit there. His blue uniform was torn at one shoulder. The
glow around his hands had faded to a faint pulse.

4
00:01:05,638 --> 00:01:27,749
The first time your body holds a charge, he said, it feels like it
should be able to hold all of it. I looked at him. It can't, he said.
Nigga, my stomach already submitted that finding. He smiled tiredly.
Then listen to your stomach. Above the tower, Voss's damaged aircraft
circled once. Smoke trailed from its left engine.

5
00:01:27,999 --> 00:01:51,801
The coupling he had stolen from the Heart glowed through the cockpit
like a little captive sun. Bell spoke over the radio. The newer
support chamber was stable. The stadium's western ring was holding.
Miriam had isolated the old tower's first two locks. One remained, and
Voss still controlled it through the stolen coupling. We have to
separate him from it, Bell said.

6
00:01:52,051 --> 00:02:15,929
Tank looked up. Nigga, separate how thoroughly? Bell paused. Enough
that he stops using it. Now that's a specification I can respect. The
aircraft descended toward the stadium. Voss was not fleeing. He had
seen people cheering beneath my car. Seen his guards stop firing. Seen
the academy move at the sound of my voice instead of his.

7
00:02:16,179 --> 00:02:39,519
The nigga could have left with a flying machine and a stolen store of
power. It wasn't enough. He wanted the people who had refused him to
watch somebody take me apart. He landed on the stadium's central
platform. The place where they handed out trophies. Some men never
understood how thoroughly location could insult them. His aircraft's
canopy opened.

8
00:02:39,769 --> 00:03:02,081
He stepped out in the black armor, the coupling fixed against his
chest. Blue force moved around him in ugly jerks. The staff was
broken, but he had turned the remaining length into a handle for the
charge. Aiden, he shouted. His voice carried through the stadium
speakers, still linked to the old tower. People stopped moving. I sat
up.

9
00:03:02,331 --> 00:03:25,083
Shawna put her hand against my chest. One more does not mean
unlimited. I covered her hand with mine. I know. Say what you're
actually going to do. I looked down at the field. At Voss standing in
the center of a school he had nearly destroyed because it had stopped
admiring him. Finish with help. She nodded. Then she opened my door.

10
00:03:25,333 --> 00:03:49,950
Tank took the driver's seat. I moved into the passenger side. Shawna
climbed onto the rear platform of a nearby rescue cart with Victor,
and Petra joined them from the stairs. Knox's officers kept the
evacuation lanes clear. Rook and the men who had abandoned Voss put
their weapons down in a visible line and helped the last spectators
leave the lower seats.

11
00:03:50,200 --> 00:04:08,862
Voss saw them. Traitors. Rook looked up at the platform. You dropped
our bridge. I gave you purpose. You gave us a long fall. Tank started
the Lamborghini. Nigga, even his employees reviewing him badly. We
drove down the stadium access road toward the field.

12
00:04:09,112 --> 00:04:27,417
The tires rolled over grass as green and perfect as if nobody had
spent the morning trying to turn it into wreckage. I looked at the
finish arch from the race. It stood above the far entrance, bent but
intact. Two days ago I had arrived beneath it in first place.

13
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:53,259
Today I intended to leave the same way, even if I had to let my
brother drive. Voss lifted his armored hand. Tank swerved before the
blast struck. Blue force tore a long groove through the turf behind
us. The Lamborghini slid sideways and came around facing the platform.
Nigga got no respect for landscaping, Tank said. Harlan gonna be
furious. Voss struck again.

14
00:04:53,509 --> 00:05:14,971
Petra stepped in front of the rescue cart and took the edge of the
blast across her marble shoulders. It drove her back three feet.
Mercedes caught the cart before it rolled into the stairs. Victor sent
a brief answering bolt at the coupling, making Voss turn away from
them. I got out of the Lamborghini. Voss smiled. At last.

15
00:05:15,221 --> 00:05:37,832
Nigga, you been looking at me all week. Without the car. I glanced at
Tank. He revved the engine. Car still here, I said. Voss lunged. He
crossed the platform in one enormous step and struck down with the
broken staff. I moved sideways, slower than I wanted, fast enough to
live. The blow smashed the edge of the trophy pedestal.

16
00:05:38,082 --> 00:06:02,991
Gold-painted stone burst across the grass. I picked up a broken piece
and hit him in the face with it. His head snapped back. Tank shouted
through the open window. Nigga used the award! It's educational. Voss
hit me across the shoulder. I fell onto the platform steps, caught the
rail, and dragged myself up before he could strike again. Pain flashed
through my ribs.

17
00:06:03,241 --> 00:06:24,200
I had no fresh body waiting under the damaged one. Blue Thunder had
not given me a replacement. He saw the weakness and came closer. That
was useful. Shawna moved behind him. Lena's voice suddenly rang across
the stadium, clear as a bell. Voss. He turned toward the sound,
searching the seats.

18
00:06:24,450 --> 00:06:45,015
Her gift carried the word from one speaker to the next, moving his
attention away from the woman approaching his blind side. Rosa stood
beside her in the upper gallery, one hand on her back. Two singers, no
longer reaching through prison walls, using the whole open sky. Shawna
reached the coupling.

19
00:06:45,265 --> 00:07:04,579
She struck its exposed latch with the broken staff head she had
recovered from the support chamber. The black casing shifted. Voss
spun toward her. I caught his arm. Current tore through my hand. Blue
woke beneath my skin. This time I knew it was limited. Knew the pain
that came after.

20
00:07:04,829 --> 00:07:27,012
Knew I was choosing a few seconds, not becoming a god with the whole
afternoon available. I spent them on his hand. The charge moved
through me and into the ground, a hard bright arc that made my teeth
ache. Voss's grip loosened. Shawna pulled the coupling free of its
chest bracket. The armor went dark. I went down on one knee.

21
00:07:27,262 --> 00:07:50,132
Shawna ran the coupling toward Victor and Bell's waiting transport
case. Voss followed her with a gun drawn from inside his coat. Nigga,
after all that machinery, he still came back to the same ugly decision
every other coward had made in front of my wife. I drew first. Drop
it. He froze. For a moment the stadium held its breath.

22
00:07:50,382 --> 00:08:13,942
The gun remained in his hand. He looked at me kneeling on the grass,
shaking, bruised, tired enough that staying upright had become work.
He thought he had found the part of greatness that could be outwaited.
Then he looked at Shawna. His weapon moved. I fired. Voss fell
backward against the broken pedestal. The gun dropped from his hand.
He tried to rise once.

23
00:08:14,192 --> 00:08:38,819
Failed. I kept my weapon steady until Knox reached him with two
officers and Vega came behind them. The doctor knelt, checked, and
looked up at me. One small shake of her head. Finished. The chancellor
was dead. The Heart's last old lock opened under Bell's control. The
stadium settled with a long, deep sound that ran through the ground
beneath my knee.

24
00:08:39,069 --> 00:08:59,761
Above us, the towers stopped leaning. The clouds resumed their proper
position below the windows. For a second nobody cheered. We listened
to the school stay in the air. Then the sound began. From the upper
gallery. From the evacuation stairs. From the helicopter crews
hovering beyond the rail.

25
00:09:00,011 --> 00:09:19,414
From the people who had been hidden beneath the academy and the people
who had arrived through a door that would never open again. Aiden.
Shawna reached me before the chant could become too large to hear her
voice inside it. Look at me. I did. You done? I looked at Voss. At the
steady towers.

26
00:09:19,664 --> 00:09:37,180
At Tank climbing out of my car with tears in his eyes and a grin too
big to hide them. Yeah. My wife put both hands on my face. Then come
back to me. I tried to stand. My legs said no. Tank caught me under
one arm. Victor caught the other.

27
00:09:37,430 --> 00:10:00,884
Between them they hauled me upright while the stadium roared louder at
the sight of us together. This nigga finally heavy, Tank said. Victor
laughed, breathless. He has always been heavy. Nigga, emotionally
ain't a lifting category. Shawna walked in front of us, making room,
keeping her eyes on mine every few steps. I could not produce one more
spark.

28
00:10:01,134 --> 00:10:24,065
Could barely lift my hand to wave. Every joint hurt. Every old injury
had returned to remind me it had paid rent before the new power moved
in. But the sky stayed up. My people stayed alive. And when we passed
the broken race arch, Tank stopped and looked at the sign still
hanging above it. FIRST PLACE. He nodded toward me.

29
00:10:24,315 --> 00:10:33,176
Nigga, even when we carrying him. I laughed so hard my ribs nearly
ended the celebration. They carried me through anyway.
